{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4562648",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 06 - Trait Variability and Selection Room\n",
    "\n",
    "**Central producer question.** Where does this herd still have meaningful variation in\n",
    "predicted genetic merit that can be used for selection, and did recent genetic progress\n",
    "improve the full distribution or mainly shift the average?\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook does not duplicate the cohort-mean, body-size, inbreeding, PCA or clustering\n",
    "analyses in notebooks 03 to 05. It looks at **distributions**: spread, tails, and how\n",
    "consistent animals are across their six breeding domains.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Terminology.** \"Variability\" here means variability in predicted genetic merit\n",
    "(EBV/GEBV/subindex values), not molecular genomic diversity. Greater variability is not\n",
    "automatically good: it can mean useful selection opportunity, inconsistent progress, or\n",
    "the presence of very weak animals. Lower variability can mean desirable consistency,\n",
    "limited future selection room, or a shared weakness.\n",
    "\n",
    "All values are genomic breeding values, not measured performance. Aggregate results only;\n",
    "no animal, sire or farm identifiers are shown. The public repo ships only\n",
    "`data/sample_synthetic.csv` (structure only); these figures reproduce on the real export.\n",
    "\n",
    "Subindex codes: PI=PROD, LTI=L-TYPE, HWI=HEALTH, RI=REPRO, MI=M-ABILITY, EI=ENVIRO."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "554f1825",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-27T15:43:19.587797Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-27T15:43:19.587036Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.013813Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.012729Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded (668, 140)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import warnings; warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd, numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "from statsmodels.stats.multitest import multipletests\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\":120,\"savefig.bbox\":\"tight\",\"figure.facecolor\":\"white\",\n",
    " \"axes.titlesize\":13,\"axes.titleweight\":\"bold\",\"axes.spines.top\":False,\n",
    " \"axes.spines.right\":False,\"axes.grid\":True,\"grid.color\":\"#E5E7EB\",\"axes.axisbelow\":True,\"font.size\":10.5})\n",
    "hits=[p for base in [Path(\".\"),Path(\"..\"),Path(\"../..\")] if base.exists()\n",
    "      for p in base.rglob(\"Master_Database*.xlsx\")]\n",
    "df=pd.read_excel(hits[0],sheet_name=\"Data\",header=1).dropna(how=\"all\") if hits else pd.read_csv(\"../data/sample_synthetic.csv\")\n",
    "df.columns=[c.strip() for c in df.columns]\n",
    "df[\"year\"]=pd.to_datetime(df[\"Birth Date\"],errors=\"coerce\").dt.year\n",
    "df[\"SireID_internal\"]=df[\"Sire Reg Number\"].astype(str)  # used only for clustered inference, never displayed\n",
    "SUB={\"PI\":\"PROD\",\"LTI\":\"L-TYPE\",\"HWI\":\"HEALTH\",\"RI\":\"REPRO\",\"MI\":\"M-ABILITY\",\"EI\":\"ENVIRO\"}\n",
    "for c in list(SUB.values())+[\"LPI\",\"Pro$\",\"Milk (kg)\",\"Fat (kg)\",\"Prot (kg)\",\"HL\",\"BMR\",\"STA\",\"BD\",\"Genomic Inb. %\",\"Inb.%\"]:\n",
    "    df[c]=pd.to_numeric(df[c],errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "print(\"Loaded\", df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "825ea29e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 1-2: Variability and selection room across the six LPI subindexes\n",
    "\n",
    "The six subindexes share a common standardized scale (proven-sire average 500, SD 100),\n",
    "so their SD, IQR and P90-P10 ranges are directly comparable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "e7a8436d",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.015750Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.015538Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.036640Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.035739Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Subindex   n  mean   SD   IQR  P90_P10  %<500  %<400  %>600\n",
      "      EI 668 477.0 90.8 114.0    235.0   63.2   19.0   10.2\n",
      "     LTI 668 629.0 85.6 124.2    224.0    7.9    0.4   65.7\n",
      "     HWI 668 514.0 79.0 106.2    200.3   44.2    6.6   13.6\n",
      "      RI 668 486.0 73.6  97.5    195.0   55.7   12.7    4.3\n",
      "      PI 668 549.0 78.2 104.0    193.3   25.6    4.6   25.6\n",
      "      MI 668 493.0 70.3  95.2    174.3   53.3    9.0    6.3\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rows=[]\n",
    "for k,col in SUB.items():\n",
    "    s=df[col].dropna()\n",
    "    rows.append({\"Subindex\":k,\"n\":len(s),\"mean\":round(s.mean(),0),\"SD\":round(s.std(),1),\n",
    "        \"IQR\":round(s.quantile(.75)-s.quantile(.25),1),\n",
    "        \"P90_P10\":round(s.quantile(.9)-s.quantile(.1),1),\n",
    "        \"%<500\":round((s<500).mean()*100,1),\"%<400\":round((s<400).mean()*100,1),\n",
    "        \"%>600\":round((s>600).mean()*100,1)})\n",
    "t=pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\"P90_P10\",ascending=False)\n",
    "print(t.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9351eb3a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reading this.** EI (ENVIRO) has the widest spread (P90-P10 = 235) but also the worst\n",
    "lower tail: 63% below 500 and 19% below 400. Its width is not \"the best opportunity\"; it\n",
    "is broad weakness. LTI (L-TYPE) is wide *and* strong (66% above 600, almost none below\n",
    "400): genuine selection room among strong candidates. RI (REPRO) is the narrowest, and\n",
    "most of its mass sits low (56% below 500): a shared weakness with limited spread to\n",
    "select from. Width and desirability are separate axes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "254c5e85",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 3: did the full distribution move, or just the average?\n",
    "\n",
    "For each trait we track P10 (weak tail), P50 (median) and P90 (strong tail) across\n",
    "cohorts with n >= 30. If P10 rises with the median, the whole distribution improved. If\n",
    "only P90 rises, gains are concentrated in the top."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "2a5fca27",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.038774Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.038168Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.089422Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.088591Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  LPI   P10   +83.5/yr | P50   +77.7/yr | P90   +58.1/yr\n",
      "  RI    P10    -5.3/yr | P50    -3.1/yr | P90    -4.4/yr\n",
      "  EI    P10    -8.0/yr | P50    -9.7/yr | P90   -13.7/yr\n",
      "  HWI   P10    +0.9/yr | P50    +6.0/yr | P90    +3.3/yr\n",
      "  Fat   P10    +6.3/yr | P50    +6.1/yr | P90    +5.6/yr\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def pct_slopes(col):\n",
    "    g=df[df.year>=2018].groupby(\"year\")[col].agg([\"size\",lambda x:x.quantile(.1),\"median\",lambda x:x.quantile(.9)])\n",
    "    g.columns=[\"n\",\"P10\",\"P50\",\"P90\"]; g=g[g.n>=30]\n",
    "    return {p:round(stats.linregress(g.index,g[p]).slope,1) for p in [\"P10\",\"P50\",\"P90\"]}, g\n",
    "for col,lbl in [(\"LPI\",\"LPI\"),(\"REPRO\",\"RI\"),(\"ENVIRO\",\"EI\"),(\"HEALTH\",\"HWI\"),(\"Fat (kg)\",\"Fat\")]:\n",
    "    sl,_=pct_slopes(col)\n",
    "    print(f\"  {lbl:5s} P10 {sl['P10']:+7.1f}/yr | P50 {sl['P50']:+7.1f}/yr | P90 {sl['P90']:+7.1f}/yr\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fdcaa810",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** LPI improved across the **entire** distribution, and the weak tail rose\n",
    "*faster* than the top (P10 +83.5/yr vs P90 +58.1/yr): recent progress reached the weakest\n",
    "animals. RI and EI moved the opposite way: every percentile fell, including the lower tail\n",
    "(RI P10 -5.3/yr, EI P10 -8.0/yr). Fat rose across all percentiles. So the herd's headline\n",
    "progress is real and broad for the production-and-type axis, while the functional domains\n",
    "declined at every level, not just on average.\n",
    "\n",
    "These are cross-sectional comparisons of surviving animals grouped by birth year and\n",
    "evaluated on one date, not formal population genetic trends. The 2018 cohort (n=13) is\n",
    "excluded from slope fits by the n>=30 filter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4a59ffab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 4: did variability itself change? (Brown-Forsythe + FDR)\n",
    "\n",
    "Median-centred Levene (Brown-Forsythe) tests per subindex across cohorts with n>=30,\n",
    "with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR across the six-subindex family."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "c1ee1a27",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.091614Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.090993Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.124903Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.124073Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  PI: raw p=0.0712  FDR=0.2135  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  LTI: raw p=0.1108  FDR=0.2216  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  HWI: raw p=0.4487  FDR=0.5906  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  RI: raw p=0.0380  FDR=0.2135  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  MI: raw p=0.5769  FDR=0.5906  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  EI: raw p=0.5906  FDR=0.5906  -> ns after FDR\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ps={}\n",
    "for k,col in SUB.items():\n",
    "    groups=[g[col].dropna().values for y,g in df[df.year>=2018].groupby(\"year\") if g[col].notna().sum()>=30]\n",
    "    ps[k]=stats.levene(*groups,center=\"median\")[1]\n",
    "keys=list(ps); rej,fdr,_,_=multipletests([ps[k] for k in keys],method=\"fdr_bh\")\n",
    "for k,f,r in zip(keys,fdr,rej):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}: raw p={ps[k]:.4f}  FDR={f:.4f}  -> {'variance differs' if r else 'ns after FDR'}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "969e5e29",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** No subindex shows a variance change that survives FDR correction (RI was\n",
    "p=0.038 raw but FDR=0.21). We therefore do **not** claim that variability changed for any\n",
    "single subindex. Observed dispersion differed somewhat across birth cohorts in the\n",
    "surviving population, but not beyond what multiple testing would produce by chance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "466a16a7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 5: lower-tail risk\n",
    "\n",
    "For a producer the weak tail is often more actionable than the mean. P10 by cohort for the\n",
    "three declining functional domains, with a sire-clustered bootstrap CI on the RI trend."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "98ac41cd",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.127218Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-27T15:43:30.126600Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-27T15:43:38.921219Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-27T15:43:38.920194Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  RI: latest P10=405, P10 slope=-5.3/yr\n",
      "  HWI: latest P10=446, P10 slope=+0.9/yr\n",
      "  EI: latest P10=384, P10 slope=-8.0/yr\n",
      "\n",
      "  RI P10 slope sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [-12.5, +7.0] (includes 0)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "d2=df[df.year>=2018].dropna(subset=[\"REPRO\",\"SireID_internal\"])[[\"year\",\"REPRO\",\"SireID_internal\"]]\n",
    "by={s:d2[d2.SireID_internal==s] for s in d2.SireID_internal.unique()}\n",
    "rng=np.random.default_rng(42); sl=[]\n",
    "for _ in range(2000):\n",
    "    pick=rng.choice(list(by),len(by),replace=True)\n",
    "    bs=pd.concat([by[s] for s in pick],ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    g=bs.groupby(\"year\")[\"REPRO\"].quantile(.1); g=g[bs.groupby(\"year\").size()>=20]\n",
    "    if len(g)>=3: sl.append(stats.linregress(g.index,g.values).slope)\n",
    "lo,hi=np.percentile(sl,[2.5,97.5])\n",
    "for k in [\"RI\",\"HWI\",\"EI\"]:\n",
    "    col=SUB[k]; g=df[df.year>=2018].groupby(\"year\")[col].agg([\"size\",lambda x:x.quantile(.1)])\n",
    "    g.columns=[\"n\",\"P10\"]; g=g[g.n>=30]\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}: latest P10={g['P10'].iloc[-1]:.0f}, P10 slope={stats.linregress(g.index,g['P10']).slope:+.1f}/yr\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n  RI P10 slope sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [{lo:+.1f}, {hi:+.1f}] (includes 0)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ba59abb0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** EI has the most persistent and deepest weak tail (latest P10 = 384, below the\n",
    "400 mark). RI's lower tail is also low (P10 ~ 405) and its point slope is negative, but the\n",
    "**sire-clustered bootstrap CI includes zero** ([-12.2, +6.5]), so the RI lower-tail decline\n",
    "is not statistically robust once family structure is respected. HWI's lower tail is roughly\n",
    "stable. A rising overall LPI does coexist with a stagnant-to-weak functional lower tail.\n",
    "\n",
    "No threshold is recommended from this descriptive analysis. If a minimum RI or EI sire\n",
    "threshold were considered, it should be **simulated in a selection-index model before\n",
    "implementation**, not set from these percentiles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c306fa9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 6: within-animal profile dispersion (cross-subindex dispersion)\n",
    "\n",
    "For each animal, the SD across its six subindexes measures how far apart its domains are.\n",
    "This is an **exploratory equal-domain diagnostic**: it is not part of the official LPI,\n",
    "which does not weight the six domains equally. Low dispersion is not automatically good, an\n",
    "animal weak in all six also has low dispersion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "f344de53",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-27T15:43:38.924028Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-27T15:43:38.923140Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-27T15:43:46.531297Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-27T15:43:46.530022Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  mean cross-subindex dispersion = 93.4\n",
      "  dispersion slope = +3.62/yr\n",
      "  sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [+2.20, +5.06] -> excludes 0: True\n",
      "\n",
      "  Of top-10% LPI animals, share with at least one subindex below 500: 87%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X=df[list(SUB.values())].dropna(); df.loc[X.index,\"disp\"]=X.std(axis=1)\n",
    "d=df[df.year>=2018].dropna(subset=[\"disp\",\"SireID_internal\"])[[\"year\",\"disp\",\"SireID_internal\"]]\n",
    "by={s:d[d.SireID_internal==s] for s in d.SireID_internal.unique()}\n",
    "sl=[]\n",
    "for _ in range(2000):\n",
    "    pick=rng.choice(list(by),len(by),replace=True)\n",
    "    bs=pd.concat([by[s] for s in pick],ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    g=bs.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean()\n",
    "    if len(g)>=3: sl.append(stats.linregress(g.index,g.values).slope)\n",
    "lo,hi=np.percentile(sl,[2.5,97.5])\n",
    "obs=stats.linregress(d.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean().index,d.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean().values).slope\n",
    "print(f\"  mean cross-subindex dispersion = {X.std(axis=1).mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  dispersion slope = {obs:+.2f}/yr\")\n",
    "print(f\"  sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [{lo:+.2f}, {hi:+.2f}] -> excludes 0: {lo>0 or hi<0}\")\n",
    "# does high LPI hide a weak subindex?\n",
    "top=df[df[\"LPI\"]>=df[\"LPI\"].quantile(.9)]\n",
    "weak=(top[list(SUB.values())]<500).any(axis=1)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n  Of top-10% LPI animals, share with at least one subindex below 500: {weak.mean()*100:.0f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7993cbd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** Cross-subindex dispersion is **rising** (+3.6/yr; sire-clustered bootstrap CI\n",
    "[+2.08, +4.99], excludes zero). Recent animals are becoming **more specialized** across\n",
    "their six domains, not more uniform. And a high LPI can hide a weak domain: a large share\n",
    "of top-decile LPI animals still fall below 500 on at least one subindex. High overall merit\n",
    "does not guarantee a balanced profile."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c859d688",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 7: producer summary\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where the herd has selection opportunity or lower-tail risk.**"
   ]
  },
